  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3003.06 Restoration of Registration Privileges.\n\n(a) Each hardship registration shall be converted to a regular registration in the event the vehicle owner submits the following to the registration section of the department:\n\n(1) A letter from the director of motor vehicles demonstrating that the person's driver license and privilege to register any motor vehicle has been restored;\n\n(2) A receipt indicating that all restoration fees have been paid; and\n\n(3) The hardship registration certificate.\n\nSource. #5027, eff 12-19-90; ss by #6296, eff 7-23-96, EXPIRED: 7-23-04\n\nNew. #8181, eff 9-25-04 (from Saf-C 3003.07); ss by #10085, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13279, eff 10-19-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3000.html"
